WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
Two pupils describe the same place.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.690
Lucía writes: una ciudad grande.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.430
Pablo writes: una gran ciudad.

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.750
Same city.

5
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.130
Same adjective.

6
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.730
But Pablo has moved it
in front of the noun,

7
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.950
and it has lost two letters.

8
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.970
So do the two phrases
mean the same thing?

9
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.330
In this mission, you'll make
adjectives agree with their nouns

10
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.570
in gender and number, so one
adjective can have four forms:

11
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.230
rojo, roja, rojos, rojas.

12
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.210
You'll see how nationalities
break the pattern,

13
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.570
and meet the few adjectives that
jump in front of the noun and

14
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.750
shrink.

15
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.270
Your mission: find out whether
moving an adjective can change

16
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.490
its meaning.
